{
 "_about": "The outfits Skyrim's humanoids are dressed in (every grown humanoid near the player is drawn as a MORDHAU character). One row per outfit, put together from MORDHAU's OWN wearables (names as in its wearable lists, without the BP_ prefix; \"\" = the first entry of that slot's list, usually nothing). class: which Skyrim people get it, by what they wear on the body: \"wears:<text>\" = everyone whose body armour's name contains that text (a standard outfit for a faction, checked first); civilian = clothes, robe = a robe, light = light armour, heavy = heavy armour; within a class the outfit is picked by the character's form id, so a person always looks the same. colour_1 / colour_2: entries of MORDHAU's Cloth colour table (item-specific tables take the same index). Baked into the local cache by tools/bake_looks.py. At most 128. verified = seen drawn in the running game. A row with class \"creature:<Name>\" is not an outfit but one of MORDHAU's Demon Horde creatures (a single model of its own on MORDHAU's character skeleton: model / colour_map / normal_map are paths in MORDHAU's content, scale is how much larger than a person MORDHAU draws it); nobody gets it by what they wear, only the Skyrim body the plugin spawns for that creature. A \"wears:\" class may give several texts separated by | (any one matching is enough); rows are tried from the top, so the more specific name goes first (\"Stormcloak Officer\" before \"Stormcloak\", \"Steel Plate\" before \"Steel Armor\"). Windhelm's guards wear the Stormcloak Cuirass in Skyrim (there is no Windhelm guard armour), so they get the stormcloak row. class \"who:<text>\" (several with |) = the outfit of a PERSON: everyone whose name contains the text, whatever they wear; checked before the \"wears:\" rows.",
